{
  "id": 340747251,
  "iid": 17940,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Protobuf-json: The enum value is used if the name of the enum value is not specified in proto",
  "description": "close #20182 \n\nTest case:\n\nModify the enum value HOME of ./test/protobuf_lang_files/user_defined_types/addressbook.proto from 1 to 3:\n```proto\n  enum PhoneType {\n    MOBILE = 0;\n    HOME = 3; // original value is 1\n    WORK = 2;\n  }\n```\n\nOpen the capture file ./test/captures/grpc_person_search_protobuf_with_image.pcapng.gz with old Wireshark, it shows the enum value HOME becomes null:\n\n![null](/uploads/a332e5f0646af5c50fdc2fb9f0645e94/null.png)\n\nAfter apply this MR, it will use the undefined value 1 instead:\n\n![not_null](/uploads/65b189515b314ed2556fccfb530ed824/not_null.png)",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2024-11-05T15:08:19.061Z",
